 6. diff b/w if let and guard let and nil coalsing

    There're 3 ways to do Optional binding

    1- nil Coalscing operator (??)

    Example:

              var number: Int?
              number = 12345
              print(number ?? "")

    2- if let binding

       If the value exist then only will execute the block of code, otherwise it will skip the code, else block is                 not required
    
    Example: 

            var number: Int?
            number  = 123

            if let: _number = number{
                print(_number)
            }

    3- guard let binding

       if the value doesn't exist, then we have to handle the else part of the same block.

    Example:

            var number: Int?
            
            guard let : _number = number{
            print(_number)
            }else{
            number = 5678
            return
            }

